does that mean what I'm  a music manager I work in showbiz like  what a war I don't get this but he  wanted me to get the meeting and he was  like all you have to do is just get it  you don't have to be involved in it  doesn't matter so I thought I needed to  put my PR hat on puff it a bit and get  Don juniors attention and I always  believed that if I got his attention I  could then get him and Emin on the phone  which I did they would then discuss  whatever they had to discuss which they  did and at the end of it Emin has since  testified or or at least told TV shows  Don Jr said if you're asking I'll do it  so I've always maintained my email  didn't get the meeting my email got his  attention and got them on the phone okay  so the meeting happened in Trump Tower  what were you expecting to happen well I  I know it's hard for people in Fez I was  expecting nothing because I wasn't  supposed to be there but it was one of  these perfect storm things where when I  got there just to take them through  security obviously they were expecting  the Trump's this is I suppose what was  in my email or whatever Hammond had told  them which was some kind of I hate using  the word dirt because it gets bandied  around and means different things but  some kind of dirt some smoking gun of  something some illegal contribution to  the Democratic candidates campaign I  didn't care what was being said because  as far as I was concerned I was meeting  these people take him into security and  saying goodbye it just so happens they  asked me if I would do the introduction  to Don Julia and then the perfect storm  completed when he said why don't you  just sit in and it's gonna be a short  meeting you can get him out at the end  so by default I now find myself in one  of the most famous meetings of all time  did the alarm bells not ring because  you're setting up a meeting between  Russians influential Russians and  someone who wants to be President of the  United States did you not think hang on  a minute maybe I should be phoning the  FBI or something like that I get asked  that a lot and and also by people  investigating this and and what I would  say to that is a lot of people go how  could Rob Goldstone a journalist from  Manchester England not know this and I  say how can Paul Manafort who was the  chairman of the Trump campaign not from  Manchester England but the chairman of  the campaign who was sitting in that  meeting why didn't he say  why didn't he flag it I had zero idea of  this but actually because it had come  from Eman who never talked politics with  me and implied that this was just a  favor his dad was doing for some random  attorney that he knew no alarm bells  went off Russia also wasn't the  hot-button subject that it is today and  you know hindsight's an amazing thing  and yes if I had to do it all over again  I will say if I have to do it all over  again with the same information I had I  would do it the same way but obviously  with hindsight of knowing yeah of course  I wouldn't send it so you're in the  meeting and in the end there wasn't  really any dirt was there what there was  I thought was a perfect example of a  bait-and-switch the dirt that she was  talking about was illegal contributions  by people like Bill Browder  and the zip brothers to the Democrats  but then she wanted to talk about the  Magnitsky Act and its actual effects on  the adoption of Russian kids it was a  sanction that Russia imposed back on  America so I dismissed this as nothing  I'd never even heard of the magnets yet  until I saw Vladimir Putin standing on a  stage I was watching TV next to Donald  Trump in Helsinki and start talking  about the Magnitsky Act and mentioned  Bill Browder by name and a kind of light  went off and I was like well wait this  isn't just important to this attorney  this is obviously important to Vladimir  Putin so the idea that this attorney  wanted the meeting for the very nature  of saying these people are outrageously  giving millions of dollars to the  Democrats that was her dirt it's just  not the dirt they expected and I suppose  what people say now again with hindsight  is that even though there wasn't a great  deal of dirt it's the very fact that  they agreed to this meeting that all of  the willingness to have the meeting yeah  and I suppose if at the beginning Don  jr. or anybody involved had said well we  were fishing or well we were doing it as  a favor it's the fact that they just I  suppose either ignored it or forgot to  report it or chose not to and then it  showed a kind of willingness that if it  was dirt  sometimes when I hear Don jr. say and  you know can you believe at the end  it was nothing I kind of want to shake  him and go shouldn't you be saying thank  goodness it was nothing because yes it  turned out to be about nothing but  that's a good thing  what still there is whether this could  be termed as opposition research but  again there was a willingness based on  what was in my email and presumably what  was in Emmons call to listen now you've  been described in the past as a useful  idiot for the Russians you've been  described as a clown someone who is  bonkers do you agree with any of that um  well some of it but I think it's until  it was an interesting one because at  first I've misread it and thought they  just said I was an idiot but then when I  when I researched it more it's a term  used it's attributed to Lenin when in  the Soviet era it was people who were  patsies who were duped into doing things  and originally I dismissed that idea I  was like ridiculous outrageous it's none  of that I did a favor but when I saw the  attorney natalia vessel 'not scious say  and i think an NBC interview i am an  informant i was like where were we an  informant to who you know my puffing  that she was a government attorney  suddenly all looked to be kind of spot  on and so as it's played out over the  last year or a year and a half  although i puffed the email I did really  well because if you look at it judging  by what's now been admitted to and found  out it's almost spot-on I just didn't  know that at the time Donald Trump has  always said there was absolutely no  conclude collusion do you agree I think  if if the definition of collusion is  based around this meeting then he's  completely right I just think that the  issue of collusion is much bigger and I  think Russia Gate is a jigsaw puzzle I  think it's a massive puzzle with lots of  pieces and I think the meeting is just  one of those pieces that may be a part  that doesn't fit and it may be a  standalone what it was was a tangible  piece of evidence partly because of my  email with the words Russia Democrats  Trump Clinton that there was a  willingness for them to look at and in  fact perhaps go further Rob go soon we  must leave it there thank you very much  indeed pleasure
 

